Description: Declare a bottle requirement the archives can satisfy
 Upstream pins "bottle == 0.13.*". noble ships 0.12.25, and PlatformIO's only
 use of bottle is the bottle.template() call in
 platformio/project/integration/generator.py, which is the same in 0.12 and
 0.13 -- so the pin becomes ">= 0.12". resolute and stonking ship 0.13.x and
 would not need this; one debian/ serves all three.
 .
 This does NOT change the binary package's dependencies, and it is worth
 saying so because the obvious assumption is that it does. dh_python3 drops
 PEP 440 version constraints when it turns install_requires into
 ${python3:Depends}: measured 2026-11-05, a noble build with and without this
 patch generated byte-identical "Depends:" lines, python3-bottle unversioned
 in both.
 .
 What it changes is the requirement metadata the installed package carries,
 in PKG-INFO's Requires-Dist and the egg-info's requires.txt. With upstream's
 pin, a platformio installed on noble declares a requirement its own system
 cannot satisfy: "pip check" reports it, and
 pkg_resources.require("platformio") raises VersionConflict. PlatformIO
 itself never reads those pins at runtime -- get_pip_dependencies() is called
 only from setup.py and from "pio upgrade", which pip-installs them and hits
 PEP 668 on a system install anyway -- so this is about not shipping a false
 statement, not about fixing a failure.
 .
 Upstream's click exclusion "!= 8.3" is deliberately left alone. It cannot be
 expressed as a dpkg dependency either, but since dh_python3 discards the
 whole constraint there is nothing to gain by rewriting it, and dropping it
 would have the package claim support for the 8.3.0 upstream excludes. No
 Ubuntu series ships 8.3.0: noble has 8.1.6, resolute 8.1.8 and stonking
 8.3.3.
